1
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,880
谢谢你的捐赠
Oh,thank you so much for the donation.

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:05,540
我希望我能帮到更多
I wish I could do more,

3
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:06,817
只是一堆过时的旧衣服
it's just a bunch of old, outdated clothes.

4
00:00:06,817 --> 00:00:08,340
一定都很不错
Oh,sure it's great.

5
00:00:09,791 --> 00:00:12,060
3个星期前 我们的邻居兰德家
3 weeks ago, our neighbours, the Rand's

6
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:15,280
在一场大火中失去了房子和一切
lost their house and everything they own in a fire.

7
00:00:15,619 --> 00:00:17,217
幸运的是没人受伤
Foetunately nobody was hurt.

8
00:00:17,217 --> 00:00:18,847
更幸运的是 有他们的朋友
And fortunately, their friends,

9
00:00:18,847 --> 00:00:19,980
就是我身边这位神奇女侠
was wonder woman, over here.

10
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:21,360
我可不是神奇女侠
I'm hardly wonder woman.

11
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:24,360
她动员了整个街区为他们捐赠衣服
She mobilized the community to donate clothes,

12
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:25,840
家具以及日常用品
furniture, appliances.

13
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:27,760
以助他们开始在新家的生活
All to help them start over in their new rental.

14
00:00:27,770 --> 00:00:30,286
-房子是你找的 -我不是神奇女侠
- Which you found them. - I'm no wonder woman.

15
00:00:30,286 --> 00:00:31,966
援助兰德计划是她的主意
Rand-aid was her idea.

16
00:00:32,384 --> 00:00:34,353
"援助兰德计划" 那囧名可不是我起的
It wasn't my idea to call it "Rand-aid."

17
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:35,760
好吧
Okay, fine.

18
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:37,580
我是神奇女侠
I'm wonder woman.

19
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:39,360
可怕的灾难
Terrible tragedy.

20
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:41,080
他们是我们最亲密的朋友
They're our closest friends.

21
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:42,040
也就认识而已
We know them.

22
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:43,789
曼尼和他们家儿子罗本关系很铁
Uh, Manny and their son Reuben are tight.

23
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,220
事实上 他们家有个衣柜是我安装的
In fact, I put in one of their closets.

24
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:45,980
我不是说有多了不起
Not that it matters,

25
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:48,100
但那是火灾中唯一幸存的东西了
but it was the only structure to survive the fire.

26
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:50,320
上帝啊 不要提"火"那个词
Por favor, don't even say that word!

27
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:53,100
在我们国家 如果房子被烧毁
In my country it is considered very, very bad luck

28
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:54,660
那就意味着背到极点
when your house burns down.

29
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:58,920
他们离我们就一个街区远
They lived a block away from us.

30
00:00:59,240 --> 00:00:59,880
到处都是烟雾
Smoke was everywhere.

31
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,360
我很难过 好几天都没睡
I was so upset, I couldn't sleep for days.

32
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:04,920
当然 米奇尔也不准我吃药
Of course, Mitchell won't let me take anything.

33
00:01:05,020 --> 00:01:06,780
小卡 我们都知道原因吧
Well, Cam, we both know why.

34
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,080
有些人吃了那药会梦游
Some people have been known to sleepwalk

35
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:11,280
甚至在梦中开车
or even sleep drive on that medication.

36
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:13,780
小卡的问题要严重的多
Cam's reaction is much worse.

37
00:01:22,621 --> 00:01:25,380
哦 哦 哦 上帝啊
Oh! Ohh! Oh, god.

38
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:28,140
我梦中扮小丑
I sleep clown.

39
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:32,720
老爸 你是在要自己的老命啊
Dad, you're gonna kill yourself.

40
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:34,360
我能行 我们还有安排
I got it! We're on a schedule here.

41
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:35,820
我还得去把卡车开过来
I still have to pick up the truck.

42
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:37,980
如果你不想让他搬东西
If you want him to stop lifting things,

43
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:39,360
就都放进杂物袋里
put all this in grocery bags

44
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:41,040
然后把电视调到足球频道
and turn the TV on to a football game.

45
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:44,280
把电话从我身上拿走
Oh! Take this phone away from me!

46
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:44,820
怎么了
Why?

47
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:47,360
我们公司最棒的两个经纪人另起炉灶了
Two of our best brokers left to start their own agency,

48
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:48,980
办公室流言蜚语四起
and the office gossip is flying.

49
00:01:49,290 --> 00:01:51,100
我今天只想关注兰德一家的事
But I want today to be about the Rands...

50
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:53,000
一旦我开始听电话 哦 上帝啊
And if I have this-- oh, my god!

51
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:55,880
那两个家伙还带走了两个秘书和管子兄
Those guys took two secretaries and the tube dude with them!

52
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:57,000
管子兄是谁
Who's the tube dude?

53
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:58,860
就是那引人注目 迎风飘舞的家伙
You know, the blowy guy that attracts all the attention.

54
00:01:58,920 --> 00:01:59,300
像这样...
This guy...

55
00:02:00,483 --> 00:02:02,140
懂了 我见过他的
Ah, si, I've seen him.

56
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:04,780
他这样下来 然后这样摇摆
He goes down over there, and then he shakes up.

57
00:02:05,140 --> 00:02:07,460
-再这样下来 -差不多就这样
- And goes down in there, and then... - You almost got it.

58
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:08,222
又这样下去
And then goes down.

59
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:11,000
抱歉 我们本该早些到的
Hi, hi, sorry. We would have been here sooner,

60
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,740
可我老公出门前不停换衣服
But this one had a wardrobe crisis.

61
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,060
那可是个很严肃的场合
You know, it's a somber occasion,

62
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:15,580
而我的上衣都太喜庆了
and all my tops are too joyful.

63
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:17,576
-你可不想遇到我们的问题 -不
-You do not want our problems. -No.

64
00:02:17,586 --> 00:02:19,070
-杰 我来帮你 -不 我行
- Oh, here, Jay, let me help. - No, I got it.

65
00:02:19,070 --> 00:02:20,964
-我的背 -爸
- Aah! My back! - Dad!

66
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:22,940
不 杰 你学得不像
No, Jay, that's not quite it.

67
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:24,440
知道吗 仿佛有一股风贯穿你全身
Remember, you got air blowing through you,

68
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:26,080
所以更像这样
So it's more like...

69
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,460
然后随风 起舞
And then out. And then out.

70
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:41,860
不要管我 我很好
Leave me alone. I'm fine.

71
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:43,642
我得去开那辆卡车
I've gotta pick up that truck.

72
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,460
我愿意去开那辆卡车
I'd be happy to get the truck.

73
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:47,740
算了吧 那卡车挺大的
I don't think so. It's a pretty big truck.

74
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:50,220
哦 难道还能大过
Oh. Is it--is it bigger than the combine

75
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:51,920
我从12岁就开始驾驶的联合收割机
I've been driving since I was 12 years old?

76
00:02:52,006 --> 00:02:54,080
或是那个巨型收割型拖拉机
Or the Widrow tractor with the Macdon header

77
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:57,300
就是我开去参加高中毕业舞会 并平行停车的那个吗
that I drove to and parallel parked at my high school prom? Hmm?

78
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:00,900
-至少那晚地面被刺"破"了 -我听到了
- At least something got plowed that night. - Heard that!

79
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:02,420
你妹的
Oh, son of bitch!

80
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:04,640
你的腰部正在痉挛呢 杰
Your low back is in spasm, Jay.

81
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:06,000
我可以给你做个按摩
I can massage that out for you.

82
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:06,620
我很好
I'm fine.

83
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:07,940
老爸 你会错过极大的享受哦
Dad, you don't know what you're missing.

84
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:09,160
菲尔简直就是魔法师
Phil is a magician.

85
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:10,720
还是个有执照的按摩师
And a licensed masseur.

86
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:13,260
在我投身房地产业之前
Before I heard the siren song of residential real estate,

87
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:15,140
我可是按摩大师哦
I was bitten by the rub bug.

88
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:16,220
他真的很神奇
No, he's--he's amazing.

89
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:17,600
之前我腿上长了个包
I had this knot in my leg,

90
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:19,060
菲尔帮我按摩了两分钟就消了
Two minutes with Phil and it was gone.

91
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:21,400
不好意思 我觉得你可能比较习惯
I'm sorry, but I think you might have a higher tolerance

92
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:23,460
让男人的手在你身上乱摸
for a man's hands on your body than I do.

93
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:26,200
-您真会说话 -不要犯傻了
- Charming. - Ay, don't be an idiot.

94
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:27,540
让菲尔帮帮你吧
Let Phil help you.

95
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:28,240
好吧
Fine.

96
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,360
太棒了 我这就去准备房间
Great! I'll just go get the room ready.

97
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,740
你会为我双手的魔力感到吃惊的
I'll think you'll be surprised with what these hands can do.

98
00:03:32,795 --> 00:03:34,740
是吗 你的双手能因为你和人打赌
Really? Can they drive a Bobcat skid-steer

99
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:36,660
就开着带草扒子的小推土机 穿越学校过道吗
with a bucket grapple through a school hallway on a dare?

100
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:39,180
我的双手不但可以 还成功了
Because these can and have.

101
00:03:42,724 --> 00:03:43,700
可怜的罗本
Poor Reuben, huh?

102
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:45,680
不得不在12岁时就重建自己的生活
Having to rebuild his whole life at age 12.

103
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:47,780
是啊 太他妈背了
Yeah. That blows.

104
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:49,260
我明白我俩都被吓坏了
I know we're both shaken up,

105
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:50,300
不过还是要注意文明用语
but let's watch the language.

106
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:53,380
把这个放到安全的地方 这是给罗本的
Okay, put this in a safe place. It's for Reuben.

107
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:55,640
就是那种
It's one of those, um,

108
00:03:55,679 --> 00:03:57,354
怎么说来着 那种塔卡塔卡响的
How do you say again, the takka-takka-takka...

109
00:03:57,354 --> 00:03:59,280
是那种内置照相机的直升飞机吗
Is that the helicopter with the camera in it...

110
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,580
可以用手机控制的那种
that you control with your phone?

111
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:01,760
是我一直想买的那种吗
The one I asked for?

112
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:04,060
是的 房子被烧了
Okay, when your house burns down,

113
00:04:04,060 --> 00:04:05,020
就得到个飞机做安慰
you get one of these.

114
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:07,200
不 我不是让你去烧房子啊
No, don't burn your house down.

115
00:04:09,438 --> 00:04:11,220
罗本是有多幸运啊
How lucky is Reuben?

116
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:12,080
太幸运了
So lucky.

117
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,480
我建议把它拿出来
You know what? I say we take this thing out

118
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,440
瞧瞧它是怎么飞的
and see how she flies.

119
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:17,560
不太好吧 这是我妈妈买给罗本的
I don't know. My mom got it for Reuben.

120
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:19,720
我们就不能分享下他的玩具吗
Oh, so now he won't even share his toys?

121
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:21,060
他从不与人分享玩具
He never does.

122
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:22,180
让那家伙去死吧
Screw that guy!

123
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:22,920
就是
Yeah!

124
00:04:23,940 --> 00:04:25,260
真是近墨者黑
You're a terrible influence.

125
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:26,720
黑黑更健康
You need me.

126
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:31,180
克莱尔 考虑到你可能还要放东西进去
Claire, in case you want to add something,

127
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:33,820
我把这箱裙子放在外面
I put the box of dresses outside

128
00:04:33,830 --> 00:04:35,913
都是爪七爪八的东西[杂七杂八]
And this is the box of snicker snackers.

129
00:04:36,485 --> 00:04:37,600
谢谢
Mm. Thanks.

130
00:04:38,220 --> 00:04:42,400
米奇尔 我们的确该放点什么进去
Mitchell, we did have something to add to this box of, um...

131
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:43,824
爪七或者是爪八
Snicker snackers.

132
00:04:44,340 --> 00:04:44,780
怎么了
What?

133
00:04:44,795 --> 00:04:46,985
英语不是她的母语
English is not her first language.

134
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:47,900
她也只是想要帮忙
She's just trying to help.

135
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:50,140
米奇尔 得了吧 你别这样
Mitchell, come on. You can't do that.

136
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:51,840
你不能突然改变规矩啊
You can't just change the rules.

137
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:53,000
我们常干这事的啊
This is what we do.

138
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,520
每当歌洛莉亚发出搞笑的口音
When Gloria says something silly,

139
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:56,660
我们就会在背后取笑她
we innocently laugh behind her back.

140
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,220
她这周过得不顺 好吗
She's had a rough week, all right?

141
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:00,820
她非常担心蒂娅·玛利娅·塞西莉娅的手术
She's really worried about Tia Maria Cecilia and that surgery.

142
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,820
而且她上普拉提课时还把手机丢了
Oh, and then she lost her cell phone at pilates.

143
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:04,880
-你怎么知道的 -我们经常一起喝咖啡
- How do you know this? - We have coffee.

144
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:06,200
经常哈
Oh. Have?

145
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:07,980
你们什么时候经常私下聚会的
So when did this become, like, a thing?

146
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:11,200
有问题吗 我们是朋友 我喜欢她
What's the big deal? We're friends. I like Gloria.

147
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:13,750
没什么大不了的
Uh, it's no big deal.

148
00:05:13,993 --> 00:05:16,037
我对她毫无意见 只不过
I have nothing against her, I just think--oh!

149
00:05:19,721 --> 00:05:20,470
这下可好
Mm. All right.

150
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:23,020
在你指责我之前 我得说 那花瓶是我送她的
So before you get all judge-y, I gave her that vase.

151
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:25,360
那是我先送给你的
After I gave it to you.

152
00:05:29,694 --> 00:05:31,445
你非得穿这件T恤吗
You couldn't part with that t-shirt?

153
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:32,740
我喜欢
I love this shirt.

154
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:35,300
你不必非得打扮成现在这样
You know, you don't have to look the way you look.

155
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:37,700
安波儿·兰德的衣服都被火灾烧没了
Amber Rand lost all her clothes in a fire,

156
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:39,640
可她得到了改头换面的机会
but she gets to build herself a new wardrobe.

157
00:05:40,699 --> 00:05:42,100
让我把你的衣服也烧了吧
Let me burn your clothes.

158
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:44,240
孩子们 快下来 还有一堆活要干呢
Girls, get down here. There's a lot of work to do.

159
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:47,300
-她要发飙了 -接下来怎么办你懂吧
- Ugh. She's in a mood. - You know what we have to do, right?

160
00:05:47,604 --> 00:05:49,646
-你不配当我的亲姐姐 -我讨厌你
- There's no way you're my real sister! - I hate you!

161
00:05:49,646 --> 00:05:50,874
-难以置信你居然 -你个自私鬼
- I can't believe you would ever-- -You're the most selfish--

162
00:05:50,874 --> 00:05:53,340
到此为止 我受不了了
Okay, that's it! I cannot take the fighting!

163
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:54,280
哪儿凉快上哪儿待着去
Just get out of the house.

164
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:56,920
这招屡试不爽
Works every time.

165
00:05:57,920 --> 00:05:59,700
知道吗 我还不想开卡车呢
You know, I don't even wanna drive the truck anymore

166
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:01,060
虽然在农场那会儿
Even though on the farm I was--

167
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:03,000
别再提农场的事了
I can't take another farm story.

168
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,114
-万岁 -你得找个人和你一起
- Yay! - You might wanna take someone with you.

169
00:06:05,114 --> 00:06:06,780
那车停在那儿都半年了
The thing's been parked there six months.

170
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:09,080
你需要洗洗车 打扫一下蜘蛛网
You're gonna want to hose it down, sweep for spiders.

171
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:11,060
好消息 姑娘们 跟小卡舅夫一起去
Good news, girls. You're going with Uncle Cam.

172
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:13,180
真棒
